            "description": "The 2020 Freightliner Cascadia 116 is a Class 8 regional and highway tractor that stands out in the used truck market for its efficient powertrain aerodynamic design and driver‑oriented features making it well suited for regional haul and lighter long‑haul operations.\r\nKey specs and highlights for used buyers\r\n• Typically powered by a Detroit DD13 engine with horsepower often around 350‑505 HP depending on configuration providing a balance of efficiency and performance for regional freight.\r\n• 12‑speed automated transmission like the Detroit DT12 that delivers smooth shifting and helps reduce driver fatigue.\r\n• 116 inch bumper to back of cab length offering a shorter overall package than larger tractors helping with maneuverability in tighter spaces while still carrying freight efficiently.\r\n• Available in day cab or sleeper configurations including mid roof or flat top sleepers to suit regional or short uninterrupted runs.\r\n• Aerodynamic exterior design with optimized bumper fairings hood and chassis fairings that help improve fuel economy and lower operating costs.\r\n• Integrated safety and driver assistance technology like adaptive cruise control active brake assist lane departure warning and other Detroit Assurance systems that enhance safety and ease of driving.\r\nOverall the 2020 Cascadia 116 is valued in used truck sales for its efficient Detroit powertrain aerodynamic efficiency flexible cab options and modern technology suite making it a versatile choice for both fleets and owner operators looking for reliable regional performance.\r\nCall Martha Servin",
