            "id": 259926339,
            "title": "2021 FORD F750 SD",
            "category": "Day Cab Trucks",
            "year": 2021,
            "manufacturer": "FORD",
            "model": "F750 SD",
            "condition": "Used",
            "description": "FOR SALE: 2021 FORD F-750 SUPER DUTY CAB & CHASSIS W/ 5TH WHEEL – NON-CDL – AUXILIARY FUEL TANK – 6.7L POWER STROKE DIESEL – ONLY 7K MILES\r\n\r\nOffered for sale is an exceptionally low-mileage 2021 Ford F-750 Super Duty Cab & Chassis equipped with a 5th wheel, auxiliary fuel tank with pump, and toolboxes, creating an extremely versatile commercial platform for equipment transport, trailer hauling, construction operations, contractors, fleet operators, agricultural businesses, and companies requiring the capability of a medium-duty truck in a compact single-axle configuration. With a highly desirable 25,999 lb GVWR, this F-750 remains below the 26,001 lb CDL threshold when operated by itself, subject to applicable licensing, trailer, and combined-weight requirements. Most importantly, this truck has traveled only 7,424 miles and has just 265 engine hours, making it an extraordinarily low-use example of Ford's commercial F-750 platform. The specification sheet also identifies the truck as having a Clean CARFAX, accident-free history, and very low miles, making this an outstanding opportunity for a buyer seeking a late-model commercial truck with minimal previous use.\r\n\r\nPower comes from Ford's proven 6.7L Power Stroke turbo diesel V8 engine producing 300 horsepower, providing the low-end torque and durability necessary for demanding commercial hauling applications. Ford's Power Stroke diesel has become one of the most recognizable engines in the Super Duty commercial lineup and provides a strong combination of performance, efficiency, and serviceability. The turbocharged eight-cylinder diesel is paired with Ford's heavy-duty TorqShift 6-speed automatic transmission, providing smooth and predictable operation while eliminating the driver fatigue associated with a manual transmission. This combination makes the truck equally practical for local commercial work, highway hauling, and applications requiring frequent maneuvering with a trailer. A 50-gallon diesel fuel tank provides substantial operating range before taking the truck's additional auxiliary fuel capacity into consideration.\r\n\r\nThe truck is configured as a 4x2 rear-wheel-drive Class 6 medium-duty chassis with a 25,999 lb GVWR. This rating is particularly attractive because it provides substantial commercial capability while remaining one pound below the 26,000 lb threshold commonly associated with heavier CDL-class trucks when operated by itself. The truck is equipped with a 10,000 lb front axle and a massive 21,000 lb rear axle, providing a heavy-duty foundation for commercial hauling. A compact 158-inch wheelbase contributes to excellent maneuverability compared with longer medium-duty trucks, making the F-750 particularly practical in yards, construction sites, industrial facilities, and other areas where a longer conventional tractor can be difficult to position.\r\n\r\nUnlike a conventional road tractor, this F-750 combines its 5th-wheel configuration with a compact single-rear-axle chassis, creating an extremely maneuverable platform for trailer movement and specialized commercial hauling. The installed fifth wheel allows the truck to connect with compatible semi-trailers, making it useful for companies that need a compact tractor-style vehicle without stepping into a traditional Class 8 tandem-axle highway tractor. This type of configuration can be particularly attractive for equipment dealers, construction companies, fleet operations, industrial facilities, and businesses that regularly reposition compatible trailers or equipment. Because CDL requirements can also be triggered by the trailer and the vehicle's GCWR, operators should determine licensing requirements based on the actual truck-and-trailer combination being used. The fifth-wheel configuration is specifically identified on the vehicle's spec sheet.\r\n\r\nAnother major advantage of this truck is its auxiliary fuel tank with an integrated pump. This equipment gives the F-750 functionality beyond simply hauling a trailer, allowing it to carry additional fuel for appropriate commercial or job-site applications. For construction companies, equipment operators, agricultural businesses, and contractors, an auxiliary fuel setup can be extremely useful for supporting machinery and equipment in the field. The truck is also equipped with toolboxes, providing dedicated storage for straps, chains, tools, fittings, safety equipment, and other supplies that operators may need throughout the workday. Together, the auxiliary fuel tank, pump, toolboxes, and fifth wheel create a highly functional commercial setup capable of supporting a broad variety of specialized operations.\r\n\r\nThe chassis utilizes Ford heavy-duty spring suspension and hydraulic brakes, providing a straightforward and serviceable configuration for medium-duty commercial use. The single-rear-axle arrangement reduces complexity compared with a tandem-axle tractor while the substantial 21,000 lb rear axle rating provides the heavy-duty foundation required for demanding applications. The truck also rides on premium all-aluminum wheels, which provide an upgraded appearance while helping reduce unsprung weight and offering excellent corrosion resistance compared with conventional steel wheels.\r\n\r\nFinished in white with a gray regular cab interior, this F-750 offers a clean and professional appearance appropriate for virtually any commercial fleet. The cab is equipped with air conditioning, cruise control, power windows, and power door locks, providing the driver with the comfort and convenience expected from a late-model commercial vehicle. The regular cab design helps keep the truck's overall dimensions compact while maximizing the available chassis area behind the cab for the fifth wheel, auxiliary fuel equipment, and storage components.\r\n\r\nWith only 7,424 original miles and an exceptionally low 265 engine hours, this 2021 Ford F-750 stands apart from the majority of used medium-duty trucks on the market. These remarkably low usage figures mean the truck has accumulated very little operating time relative to its age, making it especially attractive for a buyer who wants the advantages of a used commercial vehicle without the high mileage and extensive engine hours normally associated with fleet equipment. The specification sheet further documents a Clean CARFAX and accident-free history, reinforcing the appeal of this exceptionally low-use truck.\r\n\r\nThe combination of the 6.7L Power Stroke turbo diesel V8, 300 horsepower, Ford TorqShift 6-speed automatic transmission, 25,999 lb GVWR, 21,000 lb rear axle, compact 158-inch wheelbase, fifth-wheel setup, auxiliary fuel tank with pump, toolboxes, aluminum wheels, Clean CARFAX, accident-free history, only 7,424 miles, and just 265 engine hours makes this 2021 Ford F-750 an exceptionally unique and versatile commercial truck. Whether used for trailer hauling, equipment transport, construction support, fleet operations, or specialized commercial applications, this F-750 provides substantial capability in a compact and remarkably low-mileage package.\r\n\r\nVIN: 1FDNF7DE5MDF00913\r\nStock #: F00913\r\n\r\nWe proudly offer nationwide shipping throughout the United States and can arrange export services to Latin America, the Caribbean, South America, and destinations worldwide. Financing is available with programs starting at $0 down payment, and we offer special financing solutions for customers with challenged credit, prior credit issues, startups, bankruptcies, and limited credit history.\r\n\r\nInformation is deemed to be as accurate as possible; however, typographical errors may occur.",
